e, natural ankle and near-ground heel. Image4 shows same character's low supporting right boot from prior frame, use only as support-shape continuity, keep image1 upperbody and image1 LEFT swing leg. Real articulation of thigh/knee/ankle is required, not whole-picture shift or a detached added boot. Exactly two legs. The other LEFT leg/imageRIGHT remains lifted forward in its source folded knee pose. Foot points straight toward camera; broad toe bears weight without outward ankle roll.",
